          "aside": {
            "text": "Why does a negative power flip?",
            "slug": "indices-negative-power-flips",
            "read": [
              "$a^{-m}$ means $\\dfrac{1}{a^m}$.",
              "So $\\left(\\frac{98}{3}\\right)^{-3}$ is $1 \\div \\left(\\frac{98}{3}\\right)^{3}$.",
              "One over a fraction is that fraction flipped.",
              "So it is $\\left(\\frac{3}{98}\\right)^{3}$.",
              "**A negative power flips the fraction, and the power turns positive.**"
