          "do": [
            { "do": "write", "token": "a4", "on": "two times seven" },
            { "do": "note", "text": "98 = 2 × 49 = 2 × 7²", "near": "a4", "on": "seven squared" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "say": "In a fraction power, the bottom is the root. So the cube root of nine is nine to the power one third.",
          "asks": ["Why is a root a fraction power?", "Which number is the root?"],
          "aside": {
            "text": "Why is the bottom the root?",
            "slug": "indices-fraction-power-root",
            "read": [
              "Cube $9^{\\frac13}$: Times power gives $\\left(9^{\\frac13}\\right)^3 = 9^{\\frac13\\times3} = 9^1$.",
              "So $9^{\\frac13}$ is the number that, cubed, gives $9$.",
              "That number is the cube root of $9$.",
              "The same works for any root: $a^{\\frac1n} = \\sqrt[n]{a}$.",
              "**In a fraction power, the bottom is the root.**"
